<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chiloé</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Chiloé Island, Chiloé Archipelago</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chiloé is an island, the largest of an archipelago of the same name, off the coast of southern Chile. Settled by the Spanish in 1567, it remained a royalist stronghold after mainland Chile became independent and was annexed to Chile only in January 1826. It is known for its wooden churches, several of which are listed as a World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chiloe.jpg" alt="Chiloé" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michelle Maria · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Castro,_Chile_-_panoramio_(16).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
